{
    "title": "Rock Identifier: Stone ID",
    "description": "Simply take a photo (or upload) of rock and Rock Identifier will tell you all about it in seconds. Explore your geological surroundings, learn about different rocks, and engage with the natural world with Rock Identifier!\r\n\r\nKey features:\r\n-Easily identify thousands of rocks\r\n-Impressive identification accuracy\r\n-Rich resources to learn about rocks\r\n-Beautiful & user-friendly interface\r\n-Save all your favorite geological observations in the app\u2019s rock collection\r\n-Search function improvements allow users to search for 6000+ kinds of rock\r\n-Added more content/resources for learning about geology\r\n-Users can now add more information about each rock including place of production, date of purchase, price, and size, along with uploading local photos to their collection\r\n\r\nIdentify rocks & minerals\r\nEncounter a diversity of interesting rocks? Want to start your trial of rock hunting?\r\nTake a photo of any crystals or gemstones and get an instant accurate identification. This rock scanner app contains over 6000+ types of rocks and helps anyone who wants to recognize, examine and explore the characteristics of stones in seconds.\r\n\r\nWhether you are a geologist, mineral explorer, hobbyist, student, teacher, or just want to expand your geological knowledge of rocks, rock identifier offers the easiest and most comprehensive rock guide and instructions.\r\n\r\nCreate rock collections\r\nDisplay your properties and treasures of rock hunting, and create your personal museum of rock identifications. Now you can record your stories with stones & minerals, and easily mark down the stone id, locations, dates, purchase price, and other features of rock observations.\r\n\r\nExplore trendy stones\r\nInterested in raw stone, natural gemstones, or crystal clusters? Download this rock scanner app to figure out the mysteries of rocks all around the world. Discover fun facts about stones, such as Healing Crystals, Tumbled Stones, Birthstones, Zodiac Gemstones, and more.\r\n\r\nOne-on-one with a Geologist\r\nThis scanner app not only provides you with lively, professional knowledge of mineralogy and petrology but also offers an email service for one-on-one inquiry help.\r\n\r\nWhy Rock Identifier?\r\n\u221aIdentify stones, crystals, and minerals with a phone camera\r\n\u221a Professional handbook of geology toolkit\r\n\u221a Learn everything about rocks: name, hardness, color, luster, formula\u2026\r\n\u221a Record your rock/gem hunting with identifying app\r\n\u221a Useful educational app for geology students, teachers, and experts to learn more about mineralogy.\r\n\u221a For anyone who is interested in rocks: adventurers, mineral collectors, gem hunters.\r\n\r\nExplore, learn about, and document your geologic surroundings! Rock Identifier allows you to identify rocks with photos, explore and learn more about the geologic record, contribute your own observations, and record your journey through the geologic record.\r\n\r\nFind out more about Rock Identifier at:\r\nhttps://www.rockidentifier.com",
    "descriptionHTML": "Simply take a photo (or upload) of rock and Rock Identifier will tell you all about it in seconds. Explore your geological surroundings, learn about different rocks, and engage with the natural world with Rock Identifier!<br><br>Key features:<br>-Easily identify thousands of rocks<br>-Impressive identification accuracy<br>-Rich resources to learn about rocks<br>-Beautiful &amp; user-friendly interface<br>-Save all your favorite geological observations in the app\u2019s rock collection<br>-Search function improvements allow users to search for 6000+ kinds of rock<br>-Added more content/resources for learning about geology<br>-Users can now add more information about each rock including place of production, date of purchase, price, and size, along with uploading local photos to their collection<br><br>Identify rocks &amp; minerals<br>Encounter a diversity of interesting rocks? Want to start your trial of rock hunting?<br>Take a photo of any crystals or gemstones and get an instant accurate identification. This rock scanner app contains over 6000+ types of rocks and helps anyone who wants to recognize, examine and explore the characteristics of stones in seconds.<br><br>Whether you are a geologist, mineral explorer, hobbyist, student, teacher, or just want to expand your geological knowledge of rocks, rock identifier offers the easiest and most comprehensive rock guide and instructions.<br><br>Create rock collections<br>Display your properties and treasures of rock hunting, and create your personal museum of rock identifications. Now you can record your stories with stones &amp; minerals, and easily mark down the stone id, locations, dates, purchase price, and other features of rock observations.<br><br>Explore trendy stones<br>Interested in raw stone, natural gemstones, or crystal clusters? Download this rock scanner app to figure out the mysteries of rocks all around the world. Discover fun facts about stones, such as Healing Crystals, Tumbled Stones, Birthstones, Zodiac Gemstones, and more.<br><br>One-on-one with a Geologist<br>This scanner app not only provides you with lively, professional knowledge of mineralogy and petrology but also offers an email service for one-on-one inquiry help.<br><br>Why Rock Identifier?<br>\u221aIdentify stones, crystals, and minerals with a phone camera<br>\u221a Professional handbook of geology toolkit<br>\u221a Learn everything about rocks: name, hardness, color, luster, formula\u2026<br>\u221a Record your rock/gem hunting with identifying app<br>\u221a Useful educational app for geology students, teachers, and experts to learn more about mineralogy.<br>\u221a For anyone who is interested in rocks: adventurers, mineral collectors, gem hunters.<br><br>Explore, learn about, and document your geologic surroundings! Rock Identifier allows you to identify rocks with photos, explore and learn more about the geologic record, contribute your own observations, and record your journey through the geologic record.<br><br>Find out more about Rock Identifier at:<br>https://www.rockidentifier.com",
